  "notes": "Semester sequence, course codes, titles, and credit hours are verbatim from the official School of Nursing plan of study for the Basic (Pre-Licensure) track in the Oakland University 2024-2025 Undergraduate Catalog, Volume 3.\nCREDIT ARITHMETIC DISCREPANCY: the catalog prints '125 Total Credits' for this track, but the listed courses sum to 126. The final-semester total is printed as 12, while its courses (NRS 4026 at 5 credits, NRS 4031 at 1, nursing elective at 3, general education at 4) sum to 13. This plan uses the computed course sums (126 total); the catalog's printed totals appear to contain an arithmetic error.\nNRS 2014 Health Assessment is listed as '(0 OR 4)' credits; recorded at 4 credits with a choice note. NRS 4026 Nursing Capstone is listed as '(0 OR 5)' credits; recorded at 5 credits with a choice note.\nBIO 3520 Introduction to Human Microbiology (4) may be replaced by CDS 3300 (3) plus CDS 3310 (1); recorded as BIO 3520 with a choice note.\nPhilosophy requirement: select one of PHL 1000, 1070, 1100, 1300, 2200, 2210, or 2220 (4 credits).\nGeneral education: choose one approved course from each of Arts; Foreign Language and Culture; Formal Reasoning; Global Perspective; Literature; Natural Science and Technology; Social Science; Western Civilization; and Writing Intensive in General Education. The Writing Intensive in General Education requirement is recommended to be met with a Global Perspectives course.",
